      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Calculate ${log}_{9}⁡(27)$ without using a calculator.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=9,$ and $X=27.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ are powers of $3,$ we set $b=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{9}⁡(27) & =\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(27)}{{log}_{3}⁡(9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{3})}{{log}_{3}⁡({3}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
